cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use com-rs in your research, please cite it with these metadata."
title: "com-rs: link-level simulation of digital communication systems"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Choqueuse
    given-names: Vincent
    email: vincent.choqueuse@gmail.com
version: 0.2.0
license: MIT OR Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/com-rs/com-rs"
url: "https://com-rs.github.io/com-rs/"
abstract: >-
  Link-level simulation of digital communication systems, wireless and optical, in
  Rust with Python bindings: the blocks of a link, a parallel Monte Carlo runner whose
  results do not depend on the thread count, and declarative campaigns checked against
  the literature.
keywords:
  - digital communications
  - link-level simulation
  - Monte Carlo
  - optical communications
  - wireless communications
  - channel coding
